Basic Docker Commands

docker --version    Check Docker version
docker version       client and server version and other details
docker info         Get Docker information    general information about docker like version ,image,container, volume..
docker --help      Get help
docker run --help   For a specific command



docker images or  docker image ls   List images
docker pull nginx                   Pull an image
docker pull nginx:1.27              Specific version
docker build -t myapp:v1 .           Build an image
docker build -f Dockerfile.dev -t myapp:dev .     Using a different Dockerfile:
docker rmi myapp:v1                  Remove an image
docker rmi -f myapp:v1               Force remove an image
docker image inspect nginx           Inspect an image
docker tag myapp:v1 username/myapp:v1   Tag an image
docker save -o myapp.tar myapp:v1       Save image to a file
docker load -i myapp.tar                Load image from a file



docker run nginx   Create and start a container
docker run       	Creates + starts a new container
docker exec      	Runs a command inside an existing running container
docker run -d nginx   Run in background 
-d = detached mode.
-i → interactive → keeps input open     
-t → TTY → gives you a terminal
-t	Provides a terminal
-d	Runs in background
-i = allows you to send input/commands to the container.  It means you can type/send something into the running container through your terminal. like ls pwd 
docker inspect web       Inspect container
docker run -d --name web nginx  Give container a name
       If you don't provide a container name, Docker automatically generates a random human-readable name.
docker run -d -p 8080:80 nginx      Map ports       Host port 8080 → Container port 80
docker run -it ubuntu bash               Then Docker creates the container and immediately gives you a terminal inside it.
docker ps     List running containers
docker ps -a  List all containers
docker start web    Start a stopped container
docker stop web      Stop a container
docker restart web    Restart a container
docker rm web         Remove a container
docker rm -f web       Force remove a running container
docker logs web        Show container logs
docker logs -f web      Follow logs continuously
docker exec -it web bash    Execute a command inside a running container
docker exec -it web sh       If Bash isn't available
    -i = allows you to send input/commands to the container.
docker inspect web       Inspect container
docker top web           Show container processes 
docker stats                  Show container resource usage
